      "text": "On the shipped build: steps 13.2 → 6.7, wall clock 464.9 s → 173.1 s. In every block, all-three-on is the only arm whose interval stays below 1. Raw data and recompute commands are in [BENCHMARK.md](BENCHMARK.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why it is faster, and where it is not",
      "text": "A step costs roughly round-trip overhead × steps + decode time × output tokens + tool wait. The model is not in that equation, so this only moves programmatic quantities: fewer round trips, fewer re-reads, fewer repeated edits."
